notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Unit 42's write-up covers the worm and the phishing hypothesis. CISA's alert of September 23, 2025 covers the npm ecosystem compromise. Scott Cooper's post-mortem covers @ctrl/tinycolor. Wiz Research, ReversingLabs and Datadog Security Labs published their own analyses, Datadog's on Shai-Hulud 2.0. As the page discloses, research published by Wiz is one of its sources, and the site's author works at Wiz. The MITRE page defines T1195.002, which the page maps to stages 02 and 04.

The background slides name their own sources: the csoh.org glossary and GitHub Actions page, Microsoft Learn and MITRE ATT&CK.

