The page compares stage 06 with Nx / s1ngularity, follows the technique into Mini Shai-Hulud, and cites the debug and chalk phishing as precedent.
notes:
Three related kill chains on csoh.org, and the page's related defense topics.

At stage 06 the page compares the exfiltration with Nx / s1ngularity, where the destination was also GitHub itself. Its rotation defense points to how the late-August s1ngularity second wave played out.

At stage 07 it follows the technique into Mini Shai-Hulud / TanStack, which needed no stolen token at all.

At stage 01 it gives the phishing of the debug and chalk maintainers earlier in September 2025 as precedent for the technique Unit 42 suggested. That incident has its own kill chain, npm debug / chalk.

The four defense topics the page links are CI/CD security, GitHub Actions, non-human identity and detection engineering. CI/CD stands for continuous integration and continuous delivery.
